{
  "name": "safety-projection-visual",
  "description": "Visual verification of safety and projection systems: safety zone evacuation before blast, blast projection trajectories based on overcharge/stemming/free face/sequence, buildings/vehicles in projection path, and post-blast damage assessment.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "command": "new_game seed:42 cash:250000 staffed:true",
      "description": "#553: switched from `campaign start level:dusty_hollow` -- dusty_hollow's 96x40x96 grid put a manually-bought vehicle's grid-centre spawn far enough from the drill site to matter, and campaign start has no staffed:true equivalent anyway. staffed:true (a driller with blasting + drill_rig licence, plus an unmanned drill_rig, hired/purchased for free) is what #553's automatic drill dispatch needs to ever land an ordered hole. Cash bumped to $250,000 for headroom through the drilling wait (no income anywhere in this file) on top of the freight_warehouse/software-tier spend already here.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "new_game seed:42 cash:250000 staffed:true"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 250000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "time resume",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "time resume"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "zone status",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "zone status"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "zone clear x1:5 y1:5 x2:35 y2:35",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "zone clear x1:5 y1:5 x2:35 y2:35"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Left unmarked, confirmed not equivalent (not merely unverified): Fire.ts's Sound the Horn button (`[data-action=\"sound-horn\"]`) sends `zone clear` using `currentZone = computeDangerZone(state.drillHoles, BLAST_DANGER_MARGIN_M)` -- a rectangle derived from the live drill plan, never a player-typed one. At this point in the file state.drillHoles is empty (the file's only drill_plan step runs later), so computeDangerZone returns null, this.currentZone is null, and the horn button is disabled outright (occupants defaults to [] when zone is null, and hornBtn.disabled = occupants.length === 0) -- soundHorn() itself also no-ops on a null zone (`if (!zone) return;`). A player cannot produce this command by clicking here: not a different rectangle, but a control that doesn't work yet at this point in the scenario. (Later in the file, once the 4x4/spacing:3 grid at (20,20) exists, computeDangerZone's own padding would still produce (5,5,44,44), not this step's literal (5,5,35,35) -- so even a same-moment click would diverge from this explicit rectangle.)",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 250000
        },
        "note": "no state field exposes zone bounds/status -- proven instead by the zone status observe step's own text output"
      },
      "role": "bootstrap"
    },
    {
      "command": "zone status",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "zone status"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "build freight_warehouse at:35,25",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"build\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"freight_warehouse\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 35,
          "z": 25
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": [
          "cash"
        ],
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "drill_plan grid rows:4 cols:4 spacing:3 depth:6 start:20,20",
      "description": "Corrected from the original rows:3 cols:3 spacing:5 (which command mode ran literally, producing 9 holes): the click drags the (20,20)-(30,30) rectangle at the Drill panel's own default spacing (DEFAULT_SPACING_M=3), computing cols/rows as round(size/spacing)+1 = 4x4 = 16 holes for that same rectangle -- the command and the click were silently testing two different grids, the same class of bug already fixed in nav-cell-types-visual.json. Caught by adding expect.equals.holeCount; fixed by describing what the click actually produces. depth corrected from 8 to 6 (Ground rule #15/Finding #42's class, the whole-suite audit before Phase 3): this step never clicks the grid tool's depth stepper (data-field=\"depth\"), so the real drag always produces the panel's own 6m default regardless of what's declared. This file's own expect blocks only assert hole/charge/sequence counts around the affected blast (depth-insensitive), so this is a metadata-only correction -- verified both modes still pass unchanged. #553: spacing deliberately left at the default 3m rather than tightened like most other files' 9-16-hole grids -- a sandbox-measured trial at 2m produced a drastically more violent CATASTROPHIC blast (1259 affected voxels vs. 3m's much smaller footprint) that destroyed the freight_warehouse this file's own safety-zone premise depends on surviving. Cash bumped further ($250,000) to cover the longer drilling wait at the unmodified 3m spacing instead.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"blast\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"grid-tool\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "dragTiles",
          "x1": 20,
          "z1": 20,
          "x2": 30,
          "z2": 30
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "orderedHoleCount": 16,
          "holeCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "description": "#553: drain the ordered plan in bounded 50-tick chunks -- each chunk is followed by `event choose 0` since a `tick` command stops dead the instant a timer event fires mid-block (events.ts). Sandbox-measured landing at tick 400 (8 chunks) for this 16-hole grid with the staffed roster's single driller.",
      "interaction": [{"type": "command", "command": "tick 50"}],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [{"type": "resolveEventIfPending"}],
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "interaction": [{"type": "command", "command": "tick 50"}],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [{"type": "resolveEventIfPending"}],
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "interaction": [{"type": "command", "command": "tick 50"}],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [{"type": "resolveEventIfPending"}],
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "interaction": [{"type": "command", "command": "tick 50"}],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [{"type": "resolveEventIfPending"}],
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "interaction": [{"type": "command", "command": "tick 50"}],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [{"type": "resolveEventIfPending"}],
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "interaction": [{"type": "command", "command": "tick 50"}],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [{"type": "resolveEventIfPending"}],
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "interaction": [{"type": "command", "command": "tick 50"}],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [{"type": "resolveEventIfPending"}],
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 50",
      "description": "Eighth and final chunk — all 16 holes should have landed by now.",
      "interaction": [{"type": "command", "command": "tick 50"}],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "orderedHoleCount": 0,
          "holeCount": 16
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [{"type": "resolveEventIfPending"}],
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "charge hole:* explosive:boomite amount:8 stemming:1",
      "description": "role: player (issue #515): the Charge step's amount/stemming steppers and product-card explosive selector are real controls \u2014 this reaches the declared explosive/amount/stemming via clicks instead of Charge All using whatever the panel's fields already showed.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"2\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"select-explosive\"][data-explosive=\"boomite\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:last-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "assert",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"select-explosive\"][data-explosive=\"boomite\"][data-selected=\"true\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "assert",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"amount\"] .bsx-stepper-value",
          "property": "textContent",
          "expectedValue": "8 kg"
        },
        {
          "type": "assert",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"stemming\"] .bsx-stepper-value",
          "property": "textContent",
          "expectedValue": "1.0 m"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"charge-all\"]"
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "chargedCount": 16
        }
      },
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "sequence auto delay_step:10",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"3\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"delay-step\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"delay-step\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"delay-step\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-field=\"delay-step\"] .bsx-stepper-btn:first-child"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"auto-sequence\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "description": "Sequence's delay-step stepper now carries data-field=\"delay-step\" (Sequence.ts, matching the drill grid tool's ParamStrip.ts convention) so a click can target it unambiguously -- the Charge step's amount/stemming steppers use the same unscoped .bsx-stepper markup and stayed indistinguishable without it. 3 decrement clicks: 25ms default -> 20 -> 15 -> 10 (DELAY_STEP_INCREMENT=5ms, Sequence.ts).",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "sequencedCount": 16
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "buy_software tier:1",
      "description": "preview projections requires software tier 3+ (default tier is 0) \u2014 unlock sequentially so the projection preview actually computes instead of printing a lock message",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"4\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-tier=\"1\"] [data-action=\"buy-tier\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-tier=\"1\"] [data-action=\"buy-tier\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": [
          "cash"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "buy_software tier:2",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"4\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-tier=\"2\"] [data-action=\"buy-tier\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-tier=\"2\"] [data-action=\"buy-tier\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": [
          "cash"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "buy_software tier:3",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"4\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-tier=\"3\"] [data-action=\"buy-tier\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-tier=\"3\"] [data-action=\"buy-tier\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": [
          "cash"
        ],
        "equals": {
          "cash": 106830
        },
        "note": "Finding #36: buy_software used to leave state.finances.cash diverged from this flat field by the sum of every tier cost, fixed at the root"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "blast_preview",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"4\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"run-analysis\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 106830
        },
        "note": "a preview is read-only -- no cash or hole/charge/sequence count moves"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "preview projections",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "preview projections"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "blast",
      "timeout": 30,
      "frames": 6,
      "interval": 50,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"execute\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": ".bs-confirm-overlay .bs-btn-danger"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": ".bs-confirm-overlay .bs-btn-danger"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "[data-action=\"report-close\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "[data-action=\"report-close\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "holeCount": 0,
          "chargedCount": 0,
          "sequencedCount": 0,
          "buildingCount": 1
        },
        "decreased": [
          "ecology",
          "nuisance"
        ],
        "note": "buildingCount stays 1 -- the freight_warehouse the safety-zone/projection setup is built around survives the blast unscathed (confirmed via direct trace: HP 150/150 unchanged), which is this file's own premise about the safety zone doing its job"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "fragments",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "fragments"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "build list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "build list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "scores",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "scores"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "buildingCount": 1,
          "holeCount": 0
        }
      }
    }
  ],
